n or wait for the 2020  13 inch MacBook Pro but the hard part is  we don't really know when that will be  and then of course it is gonna cost more  money as well with all that said I still  really like the 2020 MacBook Air and I  would highly recommend the base model  for most people that don't need a ton of  power the real-world battery life is  about two hours better than the pro in  my day-to-day use it has a sharp above  average display good speakers a normal  function row of keys a with touch ID and  I know some people prefer that it has a  great trackpad a top-of-line keyboard  and it has fast 256 gigs of SSD as the  base model and has performance that does  the job well for the majority of normal  tasks and with all of that said right  now you can buy this for just nine  hundred and fifty dollars which is a  steal for a brand new 2020 MacBook now  if Apple still charged at about 1300  bucks for this I wouldn't be as thrilled  but at this price point for the base  model it is a five out of five for me  let me know your thoughts down in the  comment section and if you want the best  price check out the links in the video  description if you need to update your  website or maybe make a new one check  out Squarespace and click that circle  above to subscribe to our channel if you  want to see how this compares to the  13-inch MacBook Pro we have a comparison  right over there and also if you bought  one and it's too loud I have a video on  how to get it to run cooler and quieter  thank you guys for watching this has  been max and I will see you in the next  video  [Music]

